Section 8: The Arithmetic Instance

8.1 σ_parity and the Liouville Function

The residual generator σ_parity from Theory/Residual_integer_8.md acts on the integer lattice as the even/odd partition. Its arithmetic realization is the Liouville function:

\lambda(n) = (-1)^{\Omega(n)},

where Ω(n) counts prime factors with multiplicity. The condition λ(n) = −1 is the odd-parity class. The Dirichlet series

\sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{\lambda(n)}{n^s} = \frac{\zeta(2s)}{\zeta(s)}

places the Liouville function directly on the critical line Re(s) = 1/2 — the same locus as the waist caustic. This is not an analogy. The Liouville function is the arithmetic object that lives on the critical-line bridge.

8.2 The Verified Case

A conditionally Lean-verified proof establishes that every positive multiple of 4 is a sum of two positive integers with Liouville of value −1 (Mangerel 2024 for the the multiples-of-8 case; the CaptainS frameworkude repository for the multiples-of-4 formalization.

). This is not a proof of Goldbach. It is a verified arithmetic instance### of the parity-additive structure that the physics suite places structurally.

8.3 Companion Note

The full statement, the Lean verification reference, and the structural mapping to σ_parity are in docs/liouville_parity_instance.md (forthcoming).

---

Section 9: Source Modules

The code supporting this Part is maintained in three modules. Each is committed separately because each is designed for reuse by other layers9.1 src/manifold/endocrine_chromatin.py — separate commit

Provides the endocrine-to-chromatin writing pipeline. Key types:

· EndocrineSignal — pulse times, pulse amplitudes, ultradian step
· ChromatinChannel — per-channel tissue weight, baseline methylation, parity class (from σ_parity)
· EndocrineChromatinEngine — Takens delay embedding, Jacobian regime classification, leaky-kernel integration with multi-timescale spectrum, allostatic load computation, channel write vector

Channel count is a required constructor parameter with default 8, so the module can be reused at other scales without re-derivation. The module does not import from rheology.py; it operates on plain numpy arrays and dataclasses, so it can be used by other layers of the suite without pulling the rheology layer as a dependency.

9.2 src/manifold/eeg_hyperscan.py — separate commit

Provides the hyperscanning gate. Key types:

· SourceSpace — the 6-source hexad (P_A, V_A, C_A, P_B, V_B, C_B)
· SensorMontage — toy 16-channel montage with a distance-based lead-field
· compute_hyperscan_phase_lock — full pipeline: synthesize → forward → reconstruct → iCOH

Uses imaginary coherence (iCOH) via Welch cross-spectral density rather than raw phase-locking value. Volume conduction produces zero-lag coherence, which is purely real in the cross-spectrum; taking the imaginary part suppresses it. The lead-field is a simulation placeholder; the module's calling interface is designed so the forward/inverse operators can be replaced with an MNE-based implementation without changing the caller.

The module does not import from rheology.py. It consumes a plain dictionary of rheology outputs. This keeps it usable as a standalone analysis tool for any coherence-gating application.

9.3 src/manifold/rheology.py — extension commit

The existing ChiralManifoldRheology class is unchanged. This Part adds:

· GroupAgent dataclass — per-agent OXTR density, gap-junction coupling, NR3C1 methylation, OXTR methylation, base voltage
· HypergraphCoordinationEngine — cognitive glue matrix, hypergraph payoff, common-prior alignment, Ridge–Valley regime classification, Ridge–Valley bifurcation ratio
· Optional use_eeg_gate parameter on process_interaction_node — when True, phase-lock requires both scalar alignment and field-level iCOH above threshold; when False (default), the scalar criterion governs

The use_eeg_gate flag imports compute_hyperscan_phase_lock lazily, so the rheology module does not hard-depend on the hyperscan module. If the import fails, the scalar criterion is used and an eeg_error key is set in the result.

9.4 Integration Contract

The three modules couple only through the rheology_result dictionary. Any module can be replaced with an alternative implementation provided the dictionary keys are preserved:

· From rheology.py to eeg_hyperscan.py: dielectric_reynolds_number, cognitive_glue_index, chromatin_alignment_delta, bioelectric_alignment_delta, bioelectric_decoupled
· From eeg_hyperscan.py back to rheology.py: icoh_mean, field_phase_locked

This is the only interface. No shared constants, no shared mutable state, no import cycles.

9.5 Testing

Tests live in tests/ and are committed with their respective modules.

· test_endocrine_chromatin.py — channel-count enforcement, Takens embedding dimension checks, leaky-kernel spectrum integration, allostatic load integral
· test_eeg_hyperscan.py — Kuramoto coupling locks under high coupling; zero coupling produces iCOH below threshold; bioelectric decoupling blocks phase-lock even with high scalar alignment; volume conduction does not pass iCOH
· test_rheology.py — extended with hypergraph order-dependence, common-prior alignment, Ridge–Valley bifurcation ratio

