Section 11: The Conditional Reduction Program

11.1 What This Section Introduces

The material in §1–§10 is the biological mechanism for the game-theory bridge. The Theory/ folder contains documents that formalize the relationship between this layer and (a) the physics suite, (b) the Free Energy Principle, and (c) a proposed non-dual adaptation layer.

11.2 Theory/Residual_integer_8.md

Specifies the inheritance chain for the channel count. The document includes the notation warning: do not write 8 = 4 × (2 × 2).

11.3 Theory/Reduction_fep.md

Specifies a local, conditional reduction of QD-TER dynamics to FEP recognition dynamics. Conditional on Axioms D, S, G, C. The theorem is local in state space and linearized. Global fixed-point alignment and full nonlinear identity are explicitly not claimed. Full derivation in Theory/Reduction_fep_derivation.md.

11.4 Theory/Non_dual_adaptation.md

Proposes a Riemannian metric on the parameter space and formalizes belief updates as parallel transport of an intentionality vector. Conditional on the physics suite supplying the metric. Holonomy caveat stated. Coercion claim downgraded to detection.

11.5 Theory/CLAIMS.md

Canonical taxonomy: Axiom (inherited), Axiom (modeling), Definition, Derivation, Reduction theorem (conditional), Conjecture, Falsification test. The IDs D1–D8, M1–M11, Def1–Def6, Der1–Der5, RT1, C1–C5, FT1–FT4 are used throughout.

11.6 Theory/Consolidated_specification.md

Meta-level document governing how all other theory documents should be read. Part 0 lists physics-suite dependencies. Parts 1–3 consolidate the integer-8 inheritance, the FEP reduction, and the non-dual layer. Part 4 references CLAIMS.md. Parts 5–6 give adoption order and dependency summary.

